::ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q01::[Question ID: ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q01] [MLA Standard: MLA.A1.FN.6] A table has outputs 4, 7, 10, 13 as x increases by 1. Which model type fits best? {
=A. Linear #Correct. The first differences are constant at 3.
~B. Quadratic #Quadratic tables have constant second differences, not constant first differences.
~C. Exponential #Exponential tables have constant ratios, not constant differences.
~D. No model #The constant difference gives clear evidence for a linear model.
}

::ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q02::[Question ID: ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q02] [MLA Standard: MLA.A1.FN.6] A table has outputs 2, 6, 18, 54 as x increases by 1. Which evidence identifies the model? {
~A. The first differences are constant. #The first differences are 4, 12, and 36, so they are not constant.
=B. The ratios are constant. #Correct. Each output is multiplied by 3, so the model is exponential.
~C. The second differences are constant. #The second differences are not constant.
~D. The outputs are all even. #Even outputs do not identify the function family.
}

::ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q03::[Question ID: ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q03] [MLA Standard: MLA.A1.FN.7] Which context is best modeled by a quadratic function? {
~A. A runner travels at a constant speed. #Constant speed gives a linear relationship.
~B. A bank account grows by 4% each year. #Repeated percent growth is exponential.
=C. The area of a square changes as side length changes. #Correct. Square area is represented by \(A=s^2\).
~D. A subscription costs the same amount each month. #A fixed monthly increase is linear.
}

::ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q04::[Question ID: ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q04] [MLA Standard: MLA.A1.FN.6] Which equation is exponential? {
~A. \(y=5x+2\) #This is linear because x has power 1.
~B. \(y=x^2+5\) #This is quadratic because the variable is squared.
~C. \(y=5(x-2)^2\) #This is quadratic in vertex form.
=D. \(y=5(2)^x\) #Correct. The variable is in the exponent.
}

::ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q05::[Question ID: ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q05] [MLA Standard: MLA.A1.FN.7] A phone plan charges 25 dollars plus 10 dollars per gigabyte. Which model type is most appropriate? {
~A. Quadratic #There is no squared variable or area-like relationship.
=B. Linear #Correct. The cost increases by a constant amount per gigabyte.
~C. Exponential #There is no repeated multiplication or percent change.
~D. Random #The constant charge pattern gives a clear linear model.
}


